gible=-0.036; eligible median D_A=0.0529, median dPPP_allowed=-0.298; corr(D_A, dPPP_allowed)=+0.020; quadrants ~161-166 each", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "among 653 eligible, corr(D_A, dPPP_allowed)=+0.020; high-D_A names (Isaiah Joe 0.168, Trey Lyles 0.157) often allow more PPP", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=653 eligible of 882", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null", "observed_failure_type": "B_powered_null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-PAP-014"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-052", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-052: Play-type replacement similarity vs absorb/cascade", "score": 0.468, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-139 (0.74); FAM:SF-CHT-052 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-139"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Play-type replacement similarity vs absorb/cascade", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Having a similar-profile teammate separates absorption from cascade when a player sits.", "observed_result": "mean sim ABSORBED +0.863 vs CASCADE +0.848; Spearman(sim, -gap)=-0.19 (wrong-signed). Embiid 23-24 cascades with Reed sim 0.94.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Similarity does not separate absorption from cascade; almost always findable.", "observed_sample_and_power": "NOT_RECORDED", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null", "observed_failure_type": "B_powered_null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-005"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-CHT-032"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-CHT-086"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-092", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-092: HasConn share vs pace (possessions per 48)", "score": 0.464, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-125 (0.74); FAM:SF-APPS-092 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-125"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "HasConn share vs pace (possessions per 48)", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Connector presence slows pace (substituting half-court organization for transition).", "observed_result": "beta(HasConn share -> poss/48)=-0.86 SE=0.38 t=-2.25 p=0.0266; within-ts corr=-0.002 p=0.782. Mix: TRANSITION -0.448 pp p=0.0013; PNR +0.980 p=0.00187; CUT +1.353 p=1.2e-11; DRIVE -0.542 p=0.0206; SPOT_UP -1.248 p=0.0003 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Pace beta p=0.0266 but within-ts correlation is 0; no stint clock so poss/48 is period-implied. Mix shifts are clearer than efficiency.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=28569 periods; mix n_ts=73", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "descriptive"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-087"}]}], "n_results": 10}

